            "type": "output_text",
            "annotations": [],
            "logprobs": [],
            "text": "Yes. Tim Keller wrote *Walking with God through Pain and Suffering*, where Job is a major biblical lens for thinking about undeserved suffering. He emphasizes that Job does not receive a full explanation for his pain; instead, the book presses toward humility before God’s wisdom and a deeper encounter with God himself.\n\nI can’t verify particular Keller passages right now, so I wouldn’t want to attribute an exact claim or quotation to him. But that broad connection is consistent with his well-known approach: suffering is not necessarily evidence of personal wrongdoing, and faith can involve honest lament rather than simple answers."
          }
